00:14:56.650 --> 00:14:59.383
- Acute Myelogenous Leukemia,

269
00:14:59.384 --> 00:15:02.183
it's a cancer of the
blood and bone marrow.

270
00:15:02.184 --> 00:15:05.184
Normally, we see this in older patients,

271
00:15:05.185 --> 00:15:06.783
usually around 60 or so,

272
00:15:06.784 --> 00:15:10.552
but sometimes in people
your age, and even younger.

273
00:15:10.553 --> 00:15:13.651
In AML, the bone marrow
makes abnormal blood cells

274
00:15:13.652 --> 00:15:17.286
that don't form properly
and can't fight infection.

275
00:15:17.287 --> 00:15:20.621
These leukemia cells then crowd
out the normal blood cells

276
00:15:20.622 --> 00:15:22.721
that your body needs.

277
00:15:23.888 --> 00:15:26.320
AML can be very aggressive, so we need to

278
00:15:26.321 --> 00:15:30.088
get chemotherapy treatment
started as soon as possible.

279
00:15:30.089 --> 00:15:31.722
That okay?

280
00:15:35.956 --> 00:15:37.624
- Yeah.

281
00:15:38.891 --> 00:15:40.789
- I promise you we will get

282
00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:44.223
the best treatment plan
possible for Michael.

283
00:15:44.224 --> 00:15:47.225
He's young, he can fight this.

284
00:15:49.459 --> 00:15:51.992
- You okay?

285
00:15:51.993 --> 00:15:54.692
- Uh, yeah, dude, I need to, um,

286
00:15:55.993 --> 00:15:58.561
I need to take my pills.

287
00:16:03.195 --> 00:16:06.793
- So, uh, what's our next step, then?

288
00:16:06.794 --> 00:16:09.462
- Go home, pack your bags.

289
00:16:09.463 --> 00:16:11.895
You'll be staying here for
the duration of the treatment.

290
00:16:11.896 --> 00:16:13.861
- He has to stay here the entire time?

291
00:16:13.862 --> 00:16:15.630
- The chemotherapy treatment will make

292
00:16:15.631 --> 00:16:18.762
his immune system virtually non-existent.

293
00:16:18.763 --> 00:16:21.632
He'll be really vulnerable to infection.

294
00:16:24.565 --> 00:16:29.366
- Well, I have been wanting my own place.

295
00:16:51.503 --> 00:16:55.302
- Hello, I'm nurse Katie,
nice to meet you,

296
00:16:55.303 --> 00:16:56.570
just follow me to your room.

297
00:17:54.346 --> 00:17:55.978
- I'd like us all to take a moment

298
00:17:55.979 --> 00:17:59.480
to say a prayer for a young
man in our congregation

299
00:17:59.481 --> 00:18:01.213
going through a very challenging

300
00:18:01.214 --> 00:18:03.780
and difficult time in his life.

301
00:18:03.781 --> 00:18:05.914
Michael Boyum was recently diagnosed

302
00:18:05.915 --> 00:18:08.915
with a very aggressive form of leukemia.

303
00:18:08.916 --> 00:18:12.915
I was reminded of a verse
in Psalms, which reads,

304
00:18:12.916 --> 00:18:15.916
"Many are the afflictions
of the righteous,

305
00:18:15.917 --> 00:18:19.815
"but the Lord delivers
them out of them all."

306
00:18:19.816 --> 00:18:23.217
And I was immediately struck
by the verse that followed,

307
00:18:23.218 --> 00:18:27.285
which says, "He keeps all his bones,

308
00:18:27.286 --> 00:18:31.051
"not one of them is broken."

309
00:18:31.052 --> 00:18:33.386
This really struck a chord with me

310
00:18:33.387 --> 00:18:35.486
and I shared it with Michael's family,

311
00:18:35.487 --> 00:18:38.320
because it is in one's bones

312
00:18:38.321 --> 00:18:43.220
where things go wrong when
a person has leukemia.

313
00:18:43.221 --> 00:18:45.921
- You'll feel some pressure,

314
00:18:45.922 --> 00:18:48.955
pressure, pressure, pressure.

315
00:18:53.923 --> 00:18:55.989
- Thank you.

316
00:18:56.591 --> 00:18:59.223
- They just stuck you with a big needle.

317
00:18:59.224 --> 00:19:01.624
You don't need to say thank you.

318
00:19:02.625 --> 00:19:04.224
